# Interactive Action Form Lifecycle

Selecto Components can turn domain action metadata into a LiveComponent request,
while the host owns authorization, preview, apply, reload, and error formatting.
This workbook exercises that message boundary without starting a browser.

## Setup

```elixir
Code.require_file(Path.expand("support/bootstrap.exs", __DIR__))
SelectoLivebooksNotebookBootstrap.install_verification!()
```

## 1) Build the form from the domain action

```elixir
import ExUnit.Assertions
Code.require_file(Path.expand("support/action_fixture.exs", __DIR__))

domain = SelectoLivebooks.ActionFixture.domain()
form_action = SelectoComponents.Actions.form_action(domain.actions.record_review,
  id: :record_review, endpoint_base: "/api/actions")

assert form_action.id == "record_review"
assert form_action.preview_link == "/api/actions/record_review/preview"
assert form_action.apply_link == "/api/actions/record_review/apply"
assert form_action.required_inputs == ["accepted"]

{effective, variant} =
  SelectoComponents.Actions.effective_inputs(form_action, %{"accepted" => false})
assert variant == "needs_work"
assert Enum.map(effective, & &1["id"]) == ["accepted", "reason"]
```

## 2) Let the modal construct a preview request

`update/2` initializes defaults just as LiveView would. The event emits a host
message; it does not call an endpoint or execute a write by itself.

```elixir
{:ok, modal_socket} =
  SelectoComponents.Modal.ActionFormModal.mount(%Phoenix.LiveView.Socket{assigns: %{__changed__: %{}}})

{:ok, modal_socket} =
  SelectoComponents.Modal.ActionFormModal.update(
    %{id: "review-form", action: form_action, target: %{id: 42}, record: %{"id" => 42}},
    modal_socket
  )

assert {:noreply, previewing_socket} =
  SelectoComponents.Modal.ActionFormModal.handle_event(
    "submit_action_form",
    %{
      "intent" => "preview",
      "inputs" => %{"accepted" => "false", "reason" => "Missing packing details"}
    },
    modal_socket
  )

assert previewing_socket.assigns.submitting == "preview"
assert_receive {:selecto_action_form_submit, preview_payload}
assert preview_payload.action_id == "record_review"
assert preview_payload.request["dry_run"] == true
assert preview_payload.request["inputs"]["reason"] == "Missing packing details"
```

## 3) Route preview through host callbacks

The host can authorize each intent independently. Its result is assigned back to
the modal state in a JSON-safe envelope.

```elixir
host_socket = %Phoenix.LiveView.Socket{
  assigns: %{
    __changed__: %{},
    modal_detail_data: %{component_assigns: %{submitting: "preview"}}
  }
}

authorize = fn action_id, _request, _socket, intent ->
  if action_id == "record_review" and intent == :preview, do: :ok, else: {:error, :capability_denied}
end

preview = fn action_id, request, _socket ->
  {:ok, %{action: action_id, normalized_inputs: request["inputs"], changes: %{note: request["inputs"]["reason"]}}}
end

assert {:noreply, host_socket} =
  SelectoComponents.ActionFormHost.handle_submit(host_socket, preview_payload,
    preview: preview,
    apply: fn _, _, _ -> {:error, :unexpected_apply} end,
    authorize: authorize
  )

preview_result = host_socket.assigns.modal_detail_data.component_assigns.last_result
assert preview_result["status"] == "ok"
assert preview_result["intent"] == "preview"
assert preview_result["payload"]["changes"]["note"] == "Missing packing details"
```

## 4) Apply, reload, and surface denial

The apply callback returns an outcome. `after_apply` represents the host's data
refresh and the helper emits a message that the parent LiveView can handle.

```elixir
apply_payload = %{
  preview_payload |
  intent: "apply",
  request: preview_payload.request |> Map.put("dry_run", false) |> Map.put("confirmed", true)
}

assert {:noreply, applied_socket} =
  SelectoComponents.ActionFormHost.handle_submit(host_socket, apply_payload,
    preview: preview,
    apply: fn action_id, request, _socket ->
      {:ok, %{action: action_id, affected_rows: 1, inputs: request["inputs"]}}
    end,
    authorize: fn _, _, _, intent -> if intent == :apply, do: :ok, else: {:error, :capability_denied} end,
    after_apply: fn socket, _result -> {socket, %{reload: %{record_ids: [42]}}} end
  )

assert_receive {:selecto_action_form_applied, applied_message}
assert applied_message.reload == %{"record_ids" => [42]}
assert applied_socket.assigns.modal_detail_data.component_assigns.last_result["intent"] == "apply"

assert {:noreply, denied_socket} =
  SelectoComponents.ActionFormHost.handle_submit(host_socket, apply_payload,
    preview: preview, apply: fn _, _, _ -> {:ok, :should_not_run} end,
    authorize: fn _, _, _, _ -> {:error, :capability_denied} end
  )
assert denied_socket.assigns.modal_detail_data.component_assigns.last_error == "Action is not allowed."
```

Rendering and browser interaction still belong in a Phoenix LiveView test. This
workbook verifies the real component/host state machine and request contract.
Continue with [guarded execution](selecto_action_execution_workbook.livemd) for
the PostgreSQL apply boundary.
